1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:06,330
Two robot hands imitate the same pinch, but only one carries the cup successfully.
两只机器人手模仿同一个捏合动作，却只有一只成功搬走杯子。

2
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:09,950
Which method is better depends on what we agreed to measure.
哪种方法更好，取决于我们事先约定测什么。

3
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:14,910
A pose mapper, a contact planner, and a controller solve different problems.
姿态映射器、接触规划器和控制器，解决的是不同问题。

4
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:19,250
We need a protocol that identifies the contribution of each component.
我们需要用评测协议，分清每个组件的贡献。

5
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:23,770
Start by freezing the question, the inputs, and the definition of success.
首先固定问题、输入，以及成功的定义。

6
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:28,510
Then compare evidence at the correct layer, while retaining every failed attempt.
随后在对应层级比较证据，并保留每一次失败。

7
00:00:29,057 --> 00:00:33,617
A native experiment asks whether a paper works under its original setup.
原生实验回答：论文在原本的配置下是否有效。

8
00:00:34,097 --> 00:00:39,977
Reproduce its sensors, hand model, controller, data selection, and evaluation rules.
需要保留其传感器、手模型、控制器、数据筛选和评价规则。

9
00:00:40,417 --> 00:00:44,797
A controlled comparison asks which component works better with shared conditions.
受控比较则问：在共同条件下，哪个组件更有效。

10
00:00:45,197 --> 00:00:50,077
For example, feed identical tracked keypoints into several hand mapping objectives.
例如，把同一份追踪关键点送进不同的手部映射目标。

11
00:00:50,397 --> 00:00:55,142
That is an added benchmark, not automatically a reproduction of every original system.
这是新增基准，并不自动等于复现了每套原系统。

12
00:00:55,157 --> 00:01:00,457
List every adaptation, including extra smoothing and newly supplied object information.
列出额外平滑、新增物体信息等每项改动。

13
00:01:01,085 --> 00:01:07,245
Begin with calibrated joint mapping, fingertip position, vectors, and pinch-aware geometry.
从标定后的关节映射、指尖位置、向量和捏合几何开始。

14
00:01:07,765 --> 00:01:13,465
Next compare learned mappings, such as GeoRT, against a clearly specified optimizer.
然后将 GeoRT 等学习映射，与定义清楚的优化器比较。

15
00:01:13,925 --> 00:01:18,205
Object-aware methods add information that a hand-only baseline never receives.
物体感知方法加入了纯手部 baseline 从未得到的信息。

16
00:01:18,705 --> 00:01:23,825
Finally, physical transfer and feedback policies must be evaluated through executed motion.
最后，物理迁移和反馈策略，需要通过实际执行的运动评价。

17
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:27,790
Keep these groups visible instead of merging them into one performance ranking.
应保留这些分组，而不是合成一个性能排行榜。

18
00:01:27,805 --> 00:01:33,305
A fair comparison states whether it tests the objective, implementation, or complete system.
公平比较要说明：测试的是目标函数、实现，还是完整系统。

19
00:01:33,834 --> 00:01:38,974
Accurate human motion does not provide a unique correct robot joint configuration.
准确的人体动作，并不能给出唯一正确的机器人关节配置。

20
00:01:39,594 --> 00:01:44,634
Different finger lengths, joints, and contact surfaces change which solutions are possible.
不同的指长、关节和接触表面，会改变可行解。

21
00:01:45,114 --> 00:01:50,214
A robot reference generated by optimization inherits that optimizer and its assumptions.
优化生成的机器人参考，也继承了优化器及其假设。

22
00:01:50,854 --> 00:01:55,634
A paired gesture chosen by a person is a correspondence, not universal truth.
由人选定的配对手势，是一种对应关系，不是普适真值。

23
00:01:55,914 --> 00:02:00,839
Record whether each label was measured, reconstructed, manually selected, or simulated.
应记录每类标签来自测量、重建、人工选择，还是仿真。

24
00:02:00,854 --> 00:02:06,054
This prevents a model from appearing correct simply because it imitates its label generator.
这样才不会把模仿标签生成器本身，误当成方法正确的证明。

25
00:02:06,723 --> 00:02:13,543
ContactPose combines grasp poses, object poses, images, and thermal contact observations.
ContactPose 结合抓握姿态、物体姿态、图像和热成像接触观测。

26
00:02:14,143 --> 00:02:17,503
It helps ask where a hand touches an object during a grasp.
它帮助我们研究：抓握时，手接触了物体的哪里。

27
00:02:17,883 --> 00:02:21,383
The thermal map is not a measurement of time-varying grip forces.
这张热接触图，不是随时间变化的抓握力测量。

28
00:02:21,703 --> 00:02:27,823
Its documentation also marks unobserved surface regions as unknown, not confirmed non-contact.
其文档还把未观测表面标成未知，而不是确认没有接触。

29
00:02:28,343 --> 00:02:31,988
Respect that mask when evaluating contact precision and recall.
计算接触精确率与召回率时，要保留这一有效性掩码。

30
00:02:32,003 --> 00:02:36,943
A selected grasp subset must be identified separately from the complete dataset.
经过筛选的抓握子集，也必须与完整数据集区分。

31
00:02:37,728 --> 00:02:42,408
GRAB fits body, hand, and object motion from captured markers.
GRAB 根据采集到的标记点，拟合身体、手和物体运动。

32
00:02:43,008 --> 00:02:48,888
Its contact information is computed from reconstructed geometry, rather than measured robot forces.
其接触信息由重建几何计算得到，而非测量机器人接触力。

33
00:02:49,428 --> 00:02:54,408
OakInk2 adds bimanual manipulation and structured descriptions of complex tasks.
OakInk2 提供双手操作，以及复杂任务的结构化描述。

34
00:02:54,868 --> 00:03:00,288
ARCTIC includes two interacting hands and articulated objects with changing internal configuration.
ARCTIC 包含交互的双手，以及内部构型会变化的关节物体。

35
00:03:00,908 --> 00:03:05,993
These datasets can provide source trajectories, reconstruction targets, or task references.
这些数据可以提供源轨迹、重建目标，或任务参考。

36
00:03:06,008 --> 00:03:11,468
None automatically supplies successful robot controls for your particular hand and controller.
它们都不会自动提供适合你那只手和控制器的成功机器人控制。

37
00:03:12,139 --> 00:03:18,019
DexYCB provides images and hand-object pose annotations for perception benchmarks.
DexYCB 提供图像与手物姿态标注，用于感知基准。

38
00:03:18,539 --> 00:03:23,379
Using those human poses for retargeting does not create robot action labels.
将这些人体姿态用于重定向，并不会自动得到机器人动作标签。

39
00:03:24,219 --> 00:03:28,919
HO-Cap uses multiple RGB-D cameras and a headset during data collection.
HO-Cap 在采集时使用多台 RGB-D 相机和头戴设备。

40
00:03:29,219 --> 00:03:33,799
Its hand and object shapes and poses are produced through semi-automatic annotation.
其中手和物体的形状、姿态，通过半自动标注获得。

41
00:03:34,179 --> 00:03:39,764
Separate training, calibration, reference generation, and held-out evaluation for each experiment.
每个实验都应区分训练、标定、参考生成和留出评测的角色。

42
00:03:39,779 --> 00:03:45,559
Split by people, objects, or sequences deliberately; neighboring video frames can leak information.
应明确按人、物体或序列划分；相邻视频帧可能造成信息泄漏。

43
00:03:46,232 --> 00:03:52,112
Save the exact keypoints, timestamps, confidence values, and missing-data masks once.
首先保存完全相同的关键点、时间戳、置信度和缺失掩码。

44
00:03:52,612 --> 00:03:57,332
Every mapper receives the same stream, coordinate conventions, and scale calibration.
让所有映射器接收同一数据流、坐标约定和尺度标定。

45
00:03:57,532 --> 00:04:02,212
Freeze the robot geometry, independent joints, coupling rules, and joint limits.
固定机器人几何、独立关节、联动关系和关节限位。

46
00:04:02,372 --> 00:04:06,072
State whether the wrist is fixed, freely moving, or controlled by an arm.
说明手腕是固定、自由运动，还是由机械臂控制。

47
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:10,112
A free wrist can reduce fingertip error by moving the entire hand.
自由手腕可以通过移动整只手，降低指尖误差。

48
00:04:10,372 --> 00:04:14,512
That freedom must not appear in only one method without being explicitly reported.
这种自由度不能只给一个方法，却不明确报告。

49
00:04:15,141 --> 00:04:20,881
Give online solvers the same time budget and document initialization and stopping rules.
在线求解器应使用相同时间预算，并记录初始化与停止规则。

50
00:04:21,321 --> 00:04:27,141
Report training data, reusable pretraining, and adaptation costs separately for learned methods.
学习方法应分别报告训练数据、可复用预训练和任务适配。

51
00:04:27,521 --> 00:04:31,141
A small inference cost does not erase a large preparation cost.
推理成本很低，并不意味着准备成本消失了。

52
00:04:31,381 --> 00:04:35,921
Likewise, learning without paired robot labels does not mean learning without data.
同样，不需要配对机器人标签，不等于不需要数据。

53
00:04:36,241 --> 00:04:40,886
Include human gesture anchors and simulator-generated samples when those are required.
需要人工手势锚点和仿真样本时，也应计入。

54
00:04:40,901 --> 00:04:45,821
Freeze tuning trials and evaluate final choices on data untouched during selection.
固定调参次数，并在选择过程中从未使用的数据上测试最终配置。

55
00:04:46,469 --> 00:04:52,389
The original AKO Figure Five separates geometry errors above from task results below.
AKO 原论文 Figure 5，把上方几何误差和下方任务结果分开显示。

56
00:04:53,049 --> 00:04:58,189
Global fingertip error changes with the wrist; wrist-relative error removes that translation.
全局指尖误差会受手腕影响；腕相对误差消除了共同平移。

57
00:04:58,989 --> 00:05:03,109
Thumb-relative error focuses on the finger relationships involved in pinching.
拇指相对误差，更关注捏合涉及的手指关系。

58
00:05:03,649 --> 00:05:08,549
The figure shows why the smallest geometric error need not imply the best task result.
这张图说明：几何误差最小，并不一定意味着任务结果最好。

59
00:05:08,949 --> 00:05:13,374
Always label the frame, units, target construction, and aggregation rule.
必须标明坐标系、单位、目标构造和聚合规则。

60
00:05:13,389 --> 00:05:19,449
Evaluate independent task outcomes too, rather than scoring only the loss a method optimizes.
还要评价独立任务结果，而不是只测方法自己优化的损失。

61
00:05:20,026 --> 00:05:26,786
TopoRetarget Figure Three separates misplaced or missing contact, penetration, and overextension.
TopoRetarget Figure 3，区分接触错位、接触缺失、穿透和过度伸展。

62
00:05:27,286 --> 00:05:32,266
These are visibly different failures, so a single fingertip score cannot describe them.
这些失败在视觉上就不同，单一指尖分数无法完整描述。

63
00:05:32,526 --> 00:05:38,446
For contact F-one, specify the correspondence, distance threshold, and valid surface region.
计算接触 F1，要定义对应关系、距离阈值和有效表面区域。

64
00:05:38,846 --> 00:05:43,546
It combines contact precision and recall, but does not measure force stability.
它综合接触精确率和召回率，却不测量受力稳定性。

65
00:05:44,106 --> 00:05:47,731
Report penetration depth and how often it exceeds the chosen tolerance.
还应报告穿透深度，以及超过预定容差的频率。

66
00:05:47,746 --> 00:05:53,086
A small average can hide a brief, severe collision during a crucial contact transition.
很小的平均值，也可能掩盖关键接触切换中的短暂严重碰撞。

67
00:05:53,654 --> 00:06:00,034
Estimate joint velocity, acceleration, and jerk using the same timestamps and filtering choices.
用同样的时间戳和滤波设置，估计关节速度、加速度和 jerk。

68
00:06:00,734 --> 00:06:06,034
Jerk measures how quickly acceleration changes; noisy differentiation can inflate it.
Jerk 衡量加速度变化的快慢；带噪微分可能把它放大。

69
00:06:06,274 --> 00:06:10,774
Stronger smoothing may reduce jitter while delaying the motion an operator requested.
更强平滑可能降低抖动，却推迟操作者要求的动作。

70
00:06:11,314 --> 00:06:16,194
Measure delay from camera exposure to the robot response, not just neural inference.
延迟应从相机曝光测到机器人响应，而不只测网络推理。

71
00:06:16,594 --> 00:06:21,179
Report median and tail latency, dropouts, and timeouts on the stated hardware.
应在指定硬件上报告中位延迟、尾部延迟、掉帧和超时。

72
00:06:21,194 --> 00:06:27,054
Generation throughput, control frequency, and end-to-end delay describe different quantities.
生成吞吐、控制频率和端到端延迟，是不同的量。

73
00:06:27,763 --> 00:06:34,843
For a cup transfer, record contact, load-bearing lift, transport, placement, and release separately.
搬运杯子时，要分别记录接触、承重提起、运输、放置和释放。

74
00:06:35,223 --> 00:06:40,683
Define the required clearance, hold duration, target region, and timeout before testing.
测试前定义离地高度、保持时长、目标区域和超时条件。

75
00:06:41,183 --> 00:06:44,803
A brief lift cannot stand in for completing the entire sequence.
短暂提起，不能代替完成整个动作序列。

76
00:06:45,423 --> 00:06:51,303
Freeze object geometry, mass, friction, controller gains, and simulation settings across methods.
不同方法之间，应固定物体几何、质量、摩擦、控制增益和仿真设置。

77
00:06:51,843 --> 00:06:56,408
Artificial support forces must be removed before judging unaided physical execution.
评价无辅助物理执行之前，必须移除人为支撑力。

78
00:06:56,423 --> 00:07:02,063
Separate simulated and real results, including resets, dropped objects, and recovery attempts.
仿真和真机实验应分开报告，并包含复位、掉落和恢复尝试。

79
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:09,272
ManipTrans reports tracking errors on successful trajectories, alongside its separate success rates.
ManipTrans 在成功轨迹上报告跟踪误差，同时另外报告成功率。

80
00:07:09,732 --> 00:07:14,152
That qualification matters whenever two methods succeed on different subsets.
两种方法成功的样本子集不同时，这个限定尤其重要。

81
00:07:14,452 --> 00:07:18,952
A method can show low conditional error after failing on every difficult example.
如果困难样本全部失败，方法仍可能显示很低的条件误差。

82
00:07:19,472 --> 00:07:25,232
Keep successful-only error, overall completion rate, and the number of attempts visible together.
要同时展示仅成功样本误差、整体完成率，以及尝试次数。

83
00:07:25,652 --> 00:07:31,377
Preserve failure videos and termination reasons, rather than silently discarding unusable rollouts.
应保留失败视频和终止原因，不能默默丢掉无法使用的执行。

84
00:07:31,392 --> 00:07:37,252
If comparing errors on a shared successful subset, label that additional selection explicitly.
如果还比较共同成功子集上的误差，也要明确标注这层筛选。

85
00:07:37,998 --> 00:07:45,238
In teleoperation, people compensate for mapping errors, so operator experience affects the outcome.
遥操作中，人会补偿映射误差，因此操作者经验会影响结果。

86
00:07:45,658 --> 00:07:51,578
Report practice time, repeated trials, task order, and whether order was counterbalanced.
应报告练习时间、重复次数、任务顺序，以及是否做了顺序平衡。

87
00:07:52,098 --> 00:07:56,458
Keep camera views, visual feedback, and latency comparable across conditions.
各条件下的相机视角、视觉反馈和延迟，应尽可能一致。

88
00:07:57,198 --> 00:08:01,598
Test new people with shared occlusion, tracking noise, and initial object displacement.
测试留出的操作者，以及共同的遮挡、追踪噪声和物体初态偏移。

89
00:08:02,078 --> 00:08:06,903
Report variation across people and seeds, with uncertainty estimated at the trial level.
报告不同操作者和随机种子的波动，并在试验层面估计不确定性。

90
00:08:06,918 --> 00:08:12,218
Thousands of neighboring video frames are not thousands of independent manipulation trials.
数千个相邻视频帧，并不等于数千次独立操作试验。

91
00:08:12,897 --> 00:08:18,937
For a camera-only system, first stabilize visible hand tracking and coordinate alignment.
无穿戴摄像头系统，首先要稳定可见手部追踪和坐标对齐。

92
00:08:19,517 --> 00:08:24,737
Establish a geometric baseline, then locate the dominant failure before adding complexity.
先建立几何 baseline，再定位主要失败，决定是否增加复杂度。

93
00:08:25,277 --> 00:08:29,437
Use learned mapping when its response and preparation costs fit your deployment.
学习映射的响应与准备成本适合部署时，再选择它。

94
00:08:29,937 --> 00:08:35,777
Add object constraints for interaction errors, and feedback control for physical execution errors.
交互几何出错时加入物体约束，物理执行出错时加入反馈控制。

95
00:08:36,357 --> 00:08:41,222
Treat published best results as protocol-specific evidence, never a universal winner.
论文里的最佳结果，是特定协议下的证据，不是普适冠军。

96
00:08:41,237 --> 00:08:46,677
The useful answer is which component improves your complete task under a reproducible test.
真正有用的答案，是哪个组件在可复现测试中改善了你的完整任务。
